# Ruin Arm dialogue/menu font, 16x16 1bpp at $9F8000 (docs/re/text.md). One 16-bit little-endian word per glyph:
# key = the two ROM bytes (code 0x0123 is stored 23 01). Control words ($8000+) are handled by the extractor, not here.
# Second copies of a glyph get a distinct value (光₂, 将₂, ｡, ｢｣) so decode -> encode stays byte-exact.
# Half-width menu cells (two narrow letters in one 16px cell, $274-$2BD, $34A-$351, $354) use half-width kana.
